cmake: Test compiler flags with "/WX /options:strict" instead of -Werror

bitcoin/bitcoin#31507 dropped MSVC support and tests compiler flags with
-Werror only. cl.exe merely warns about an unknown option, so with
-Werror every flag check passes and every Clang/GCC warning flag gets
appended. With "/WX /options:strict", unknown options are errors and the
checks work.

Applied by .github/workflows/windows-cl-x86_64.yml.

diff --git a/cmake/module/TryAppendCXXFlags.cmake b/cmake/module/TryAppendCXXFlags.cmake
index c23735c..d4c2f87 100644
--- a/cmake/module/TryAppendCXXFlags.cmake
+++ b/cmake/module/TryAppendCXXFlags.cmake
@@ -119,4 +119,4 @@ function(try_append_cxx_flags flags)
   endif()
 endfunction()
 
-try_append_cxx_flags("-Werror" VAR working_compiler_werror_flag SKIP_LINK)
+try_append_cxx_flags("/WX /options:strict" VAR working_compiler_werror_flag SKIP_LINK)
